SUMMARY: The manuscript fails one hard deterministic gate â€” body-too-short at 524 words against a 600-word minimum â€” and carries secondary quality defects in frontmatter: description and summary are identical and both exceed their respective targets, the koios.tweet field is absent, and the SEO term "rights" is missing from the lede. The factual claims are supported, the two source events are kept structurally distinct, and the collapse frame is applied without overclaiming. The piece is restorable: the reporting packet contains an attributable named quote and EMRIP meeting specifics that the writer did not use.

FINDINGS: The body is 524 words; the hard gate requires â‰¥ 600. The description field runs approximately 290 characters against a ~120-character target. The summary field is the identical text (~77 words), duplicating the description verbatim and exceeding the 40â€“70 word window. The koios section carries no tweet field. The SEO term is "indigenous land rights"; the lede contains "indigenous" and "lands" but not "rights," so the seo-lede gate likely also fails on a full run. The Vancouver/World Cup source (ictnews-org-6f0ff136) appears in frontmatter references but has no role in the article and should not have been selected as a candidate reference. Most substantively, the ICT News source summary contains a named, attributable quote â€” Binota Moy Dhamai, identified as Tripura from the Chittagong Hill Tracts in Bangladesh and former chair of EMRIP, saying "Climate change, militarization, extractivism, and legal marginalization reinforce one another" â€” that the draft never uses. This is the primary omission: a named source speaking directly to the article's thesis was available and ignored.

CLAIM AUDIT: "More than 100 countries adopted the UN Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples" is supported by the ICT News source ("nearly 20 years since more than 100 countries adopted"). The storm, drought, and rising-seas formulation mirrors the source language closely and is properly attributed via inline citation. "Dying by the hundreds in wars and while defending that same ground" reflects the source's "continue dying by the hundreds in wars and while defending their lands" and is attributed. "Persecuted by government officials" is source-supported. The Nepal/Newar/Khokana characterization matches the Cultural Survival source and is cited. The claim that state development pressure against indigenous territorial claims "is not a regional exception" is editorial synthesis presented as analysis, not as a sourced fact, which is acceptable in this register. No invented numbers, no unsupported causal chains, no flattening of distinct peoples or regions into a false single analogy â€” the Nepal case is held structurally separate from the Geneva gathering throughout.

REQUIRED REPAIRS: (1) Expand the body by at least 76 words drawing from available source material â€” specifically the Dhamai quote with full attribution and the EMRIP meeting context (19th annual gathering, hundreds of Indigenous delegates, Geneva). (2) Land "rights" in the lede paragraph to satisfy the seo-lede gate. (3) Replace the duplicate description/summary with two distinct fields at their proper targets: description ~120 characters, summary ~50 words. (4) Add a koios.tweet field. (5) Remove ictnews-org-6f0ff136 from frontmatter references; it is not cited in the body and is substantively irrelevant to the article.

PIPELINE EVIDENCE: The DETERMINISTIC STANDARDS report a single gate error, body-too-short. The production run is null, so there is no historical trace to reconcile. The research packet selected four sources; the ICT News EMRIP story is the primary source and contains more usable material than the writer extracted. The Vancouver story entered the packet through keyword matching on "indigenous" and "land" and "rights" but is topically irrelevant; its selection score of 57 was tied with the EMRIP story's, and the assignment lens did not filter it out. The writer model produced an under-length draft without exhausting the named attributions in the packet.

PIPELINE IMPROVEMENT: The writer model had an adequate packet and left a named attributed source unused while generating a draft that falls 76 words short of the minimum. The Dhamai quote and the EMRIP session specifics are exactly the kind of grounded, named detail the publication's voice requires; including them would have cleared the length gate and improved the piece's evidentiary texture. A pre-submission check that flags named attributable sources present in the packet but absent from the draft would catch this class of omission before it reaches the editor layer. Separately, the source-selection step admitted a topically irrelevant source (the Vancouver sports piece) into the candidate references; the selection filter should weight semantic relevance to the assignment term more heavily than raw keyword overlap when a source's domain or title signals clear topical mismatch.

